{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>We remember the fish.</b> The language of וידגו לרוב, 'they shall swarm [like fish] in the abundance of the land' — קרישינס\"ה in the vernacular. And afterward it explains: את הקשואים ואת האבטחים [the cucumbers and the melons]."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Aramaic/Old French loanword קרישינס\"ה could not be identified with certainty; it appears to be an Old French gloss on the phrase וידגו לרוב. The syntax of the note is somewhat compressed; 'and afterward it explains' likely refers to the verse proceeding to list vegetables."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:06.996324084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}